      abbreviations: ["ABG", "VBG", "TCO2", "PvCO2", "PaCO2", "HCO3"],
      definition: "An arterial blood gas directly measures arterial pH, PaCO2, and PaO2, whereas a venous blood gas measures venous pH and PvCO2 after tissue metabolism has added CO2 and removed oxygen. VBG pH can often support initial acid-base assessment, but venous PCO2 has wider agreement limits and cannot simply be relabeled PaCO2. Serum total carbon dioxide is a chemistry measurement composed mostly of bicarbonate; blood-gas bicarbonate is usually calculated from pH and PCO2, so the two are related but not analytically identical.",
